{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/references/05_dependent_names",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "references",
  "title": "Dependent names",
  "summary": "Dependent names resolve through known primary templates",
  "prose": "Dependent members of a known template (`Box<T>`) resolve to the primary\ntemplate's declarations and keep their kinds. Members of a bare template\nparameter have no candidate declaration: they are `unknown`, or a type\nafter `typename`. Every dependent name carries `dependent`.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#154",
    "clangd#297"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename T>\nstruct Box {\n    using value_type = int;\n    static void reset();\n    int size() const;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid resolved(Box<T> box) {\n    typename Box<T>::value_type item;\n    Box<T>::reset();\n    box.size();\n}\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid unresolved(T value) {\n    typename T::value_type item;\n    T::reset();\n    value.size();\n}\n",
